    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nWhen nesting parentheses like shown below and using <motion>ab with the cursor on the first opening parentheses, the inner set of parentheses is selected. Is this a bug or the intended behaviour?\r\n\r\n(()\r\n)\r\n\r\nMotion: vab\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.10.2\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. position cursor on first parentheses in the following expression:\r\n(()\r\n)\r\n\r\n3: vab\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n(()\r\n)\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n()",
