    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, this is an intended behavior with the default 'cover_or_next' search method. It first [searches in current line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/0a8a1072137d916406507c941698a4bfa9dbbe7a/doc/mini-ai.txt#L453-L456) and only then tries to search in the neighborhood.\r\n\r\nTo always select covering textobject, use `config.search_method = 'cover'` and use `in` / `an` / `il` / `al` keys to search \"next\" and \"last\" textobjects.",
